  "title": "Visiting the Graves of the Faithful Believers",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "MERITS OF VISITING THE TOMBS OF FAITHFUL BELIEVERS\n\nThe trustworthy and sublime Shaykh Ja’far ibn Qawlawayh al-Qummi reports ‘Amr ibn ‘Uthman al-Razi as saying that he heard Imam Abu’l-Hasan Musa ibn Ja’far, peace be upon him, saying, “Whoever is unable to visit us, may visit the righteous adherents of us. If he does so, he will be endued with the reward of visiting us. Likewise, whoever is unable to connect us, may connect the righteous adherents of us. If he does so, he will also be endued with the reward of connecting us.”\n\nThrough an authentic chain of authority, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Yahya al-Ash’ari is reported to have said, “I was in Fayd (a station on the way of Makkah) when I accompanied ‘Ali ibn Bilal in visiting the grave of Muhammad ibn Isma’il ibn Buzaygh. ‘Ali related to me, saying: The one buried in this grave told me that Imam al-Rida (‘a) said, ‘Whoever comes to the graves of his brother-in-faith and puts his hand on the grave and recites Surah al-Qadr (No. 97) seven times, will be secured on the Great Horror Day.”\n\nAccording to another tradition, the statement, ‘... and directs his face towards the kiblah direction...’ is added.\n\nFrom the apparent point of this tradition, we may understand that security on the Resurrection Day will be for the one who recites that Surah (i.e. the visitor of the grave) although it is probable that the one intended may be the visited one. This meaning is supported by a coming report of Sayyid Ibn Tawus:\n\nIn the book of Kamil al-Ziyarah, it is reported through a valid chain of authority that ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn Abu-’Abdullah asked Imam al-Sadiq (‘a) to teach him how to put his hands of the graves of Muslims. Teaching him, the Imam (‘a) put his hand on the ground while facing the kiblah direction.\n\nThrough an authentic chain of authority, ‘Abdullah ibn Sinan has reported that he asked Imam al-Sadiq (‘a) to teach him how to salute the inhabitants in graves. The Imam (‘a) replied that he might say the following words:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰىۤ اَهْلِ الدِّيَارِ مِنَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ وَ الْمُسْلِمِيْنَ اَنْتُمْ لَنَا فَرَطٌ وَ نَحْنُ اِنْ شَاۤءَ اللّٰهُ بِكُمْ لَاحِقُوْنَ.\nAALSALAAMU A'ALAAAA AAHLI ALDIYAARI MINA ALMU'MINIYNA WA ALMUSLIMIYNA AANTUM LANAA FARATUN WA NAHNU AIN SHAA'A U BIKUM LAAHIQUWNA.\nMERITS OF VISITING THE TOMBS OF FAITHFUL BELIEVERS\nاَللّٰهُمَّ رَبَّ هٰذِهِ الْاَرْوَاحِ الْفَانِيَةِ وَ الْاَجْسَادِ الْبَالِيَةِ وَ الْعِظَامِ النَّخِرَةِ الَّتِيْ خَرَجَتْ مِنَ الدُّنْيَا وَ هِيَ بِكَ مُؤْمِنَةٌ اَدْخِلْ عَلَيْهِمْ رُوْحًا مِنْكَ وَ سَلَامًا مِنِّيْ\nAALLAAHUMA RABA HAADHIHI ALAARWAAHI ALFAANIYAHI WA ALAAJSAADI ALBAALIYAHI WA ALA'IZAAMI ALNAKHIRAHI ALATIY KHARAJAT MINA ALDUNYAA WA HIYA BIKA MU'MINAHUN AADKHIL A'ALAYHIM RUWHANA MINKA WA SALAAMANA MINIY\nThe trustworthy and sublime Shaykh Ja’far ibn Qawlawayh alQummi reports ‘Amr ibn ‘Uthman alRazi as saying that he heard Imam Abu’lHasan Musa ibn Ja’far, peace be upon him, saying, “Whoever is unable to visit us, may visit the righteous adherents of us. If he does so, he will be endued with the reward of visiting us. Likewise, whoever is unable to connect us, may connect the righteous adherents of us. If he does so, he will also be endued with the reward of connecting us.”\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰىۤ اَهْلِ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ مِنْ اَهْلِ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ يَا اَهْلَ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ بِحَقِّ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ كَيْفَ وَجَدْتُمْ قَوْلَ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ مِنْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ يَا لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ بِحَقِّ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ اِغْفِرْ لِمَنْ قَالَ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ وَ احْشُرْنَا فِيْ زُمْرَةِ مَنْ قَالَ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اللّٰهُ مُحَمَّدٌ رَسُوْلُ اللّٰهِ عَلِيٌّ وَلِيُّ اللّٰهِ.\nAALSALAAMU A'ALAAAA AAHLI LAA AILAAHA AILAA U MIN AAHLI LAA AILAAHA AILAA U YAA AAHLA LAA AILAAHA AILAA U BIHAQI LAA AILAAHA AILAA U KAYFA WAJADTUM QAWLA LAA AILAAHA AILAA U MIN LAA AILAAHA AILAA U YAA LAA AILAAHA AILAA U BIHAQI LAA AILAAHA AILAA U AIGHFIR LIMAN QAALA LAA AILAAHA AILAA U WA AHSHURNAA FIY ZUMRAHI MAN QAALA LAA AILAAHA AILAA U MUHAMADUN RASUWLU I A'ALIYUN WALIYU I.\nThrough an authentic chain of authority, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Yahya alAsh’ari is reported to have said, “I was in Fayd (a station on the way of Makkah) when I accompanied ‘Ali ibn Bilal in visiting the grave of Muhammad ibn Isma’il ibn Buzaygh. ‘Ali related to me, saying: The one buried in this grave told me that Imam alRida (‘a) said, ‘Whoever comes to the graves of his brotherinfaith and puts his hand on the grave and recites Surah alQadr (No. 97) seven times, will be secured on the Great Horror Day.”\nاَللّٰهُمَّ وَلِّهِمْ مَا تَوَلَّوْا وَ احْشُرْهُمْ مَعَ مَنْ اَحَبُّوْا.\nAALLAAHUMA WALIHIM MAA TAWALAWA WA AHSHURHUM MAA'A MAN AAHABUWA.\nAccording to another tradition, the statement, ‘... and directs his face towards the kiblah direction...’ is added.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ ارْحَمْ غُرْبَتَهٗ وَ صِلْ وَحْدَتَهٗ وَ اٰنِسْ وَحْشَتَهٗ وَ اٰمِنْ رَوْعَتَهٗ وَ اَسْكِنْ اِلَيْهِ مِنْ رَحْمَتِكَ رَحْمَةً يَسْتَغْنِيْ بِهَا عَنْ رَحْمَةِ مَنْ سِوَاكَ وَ اَلْحِقْهُ بِمَنْ كَانَ يَتَوَلَّاهُ\nAALLAAHUMA ARHAM GHURBATAHU WA SIL WAHDATAHU WA AAANIS WAHSHATAHU WA AAAMIN RAWA'ATAHU WA AASKIN AILAYHI MIN RAHMATIKA RAHMAHAN YASTAGHNIY BIHAA A'AN RAHMAHI MAN SIWAAKA WA AALHIQHU BIMAN KAANA YATAWALAAHU\nFrom the apparent point of this tradition, we may understand that security on the Resurrection Day will be for the one who recites that Surah (i.e. the visitor of the grave) although it is probable that the one intended may be the visited one. This meaning is supported by a coming report of Sayyid Ibn Tawus:"
